{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through both. “Nontrivial” is the model-checking term (a strongly connected component with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least one edge, as in Büchi-automaton emptiness checks); this is NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"strongly_connected_components","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" filtered to ","type":"text"},{"code":"len(c) > 1 or G.has_edge(v, v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{